  "qualitative_observations": [
    "EN: 6/6 surfaces render with html lang=en, dir=ltr, sidebar intact (left, width 260px). No raw i18n keys. Mostly translated; some hardcoded FR remains in dashboard widget labels (Vue d'ensemble, Suivi en direct, Alertes SLA, Répartition par Canal), table headers (Heure, N°commande, Source), action chips (Filtrer, Exporter, Actif), and a few sidebar entries (Caisse, Catalogue, Attributs Produits, Ingredients, Commandes Caisse, Écran Cuisine, Suivi Client, Équipe). This is hardcoded text not wrapped in $t() — not a label-key bug. V1 LOCAL Le Cayenne is FR-only by ADR-007; partial EN coverage is acceptable but worth a backlog item to scope full-en sweep if SaaS path is ever activated.",
    "AR: 6/6 surfaces render with html lang=ar, dir=rtl. Sidebar successfully flips to right side (RTL layout works). Arabic labels render correctly on dashboard (إصباح الخير, نظرة عامة, اجمالي المبيعات, اجمالي الطلبات, اجمالي العناصر القائمة), items (العناصر, الاسم, السعر, الضريبة), delivery-boys (فتيان التوصيل, الحالة, نشط, حفظ, إغلاق). Numbers display correctly using Latin digits (870,00 €, 2, 45, +33). Some hardcoded FR text persists (same scope as EN). No raw i18n keys remain. RTL doesn't break grid/card layouts.",
    "html_dir=rtl correctly toggled by i18n.js watcher (line 122-125) when locale changes to ar. Verified on dashboard, items, cash-overview, delivery-boys (sidebar_geometry confirms sidebar position changes). Stock and Orders surfaces returned short body text (~224 chars) — likely a permission-gated route showing access-denied skeleton; not an i18n-specific issue.",
    "NF525 audit_logs action codes (user.login, cash.movement.recorded, order.counter_payment_confirmed, etc.) render as raw strings on dashboard AuditTrailComponent.vue:27 by design. These are canonical event identifiers stored in audit_logs.action for HMAC chain integrity — NOT i18n keys. Whitelisted in raw-label detector to avoid false positives."
  ],
  "architectural_consequence_for_v1": "V1 LOCAL Le Cayenne is FR-only — the FR-lock at module load (i18n.js:84-101) is documented as ADR-007 NF525 hardening. The in-session locale switcher works empirically via direct $i18n.locale mutation (what BackendNavbarComponent.changeLanguage does) but each page reload snaps back to FR. EN and AR rendering does NOT break the UI; layout, RTL flip, numbers, and core widgets all work. Backlog item: if V2 SaaS multi-tenant SaaS exposes language switch to operators, the dashboard hardcoded-FR strings need a $t() sweep.",
  "files_referenced": [
    "resources/js/i18n.js:54-125 (FR-lock + watcher)",
    "resources/js/components/layouts/backend/BackendNavbarComponent.vue:53-69,275-279,466-473 (header switcher)",
    "resources/js/components/admin/dashboard/AuditTrailComponent.vue:27 (raw NF525 codes by design)",
    "app/Http/Middleware/localization.php (backend ?locale=xx detection)",
    "lang/{fr,en,ar}/* (PHP server-side translation files — same key inventory)",
    "resources/js/languages/{fr,en,ar}.json (Vue-side message bundles, ~2000 lines each)"
